From 8790c186689c68ab7bb36a61c6abf3387ca36376 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:45:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the java/vendorjdk extractor for standalone vendor
 runtimes

Glue around the static detector of github.com/bell-sw/osv-internal/vendorjdk.
The extractor triggers on the detector's candidate files - the JVM library
(libjvm.so / libjvm.dylib / jvm.dll), the release file and rt.jar - and
reports one package per runtime home; name, version, ecosystem
("<JDK family>:<major>" / "<NIK family>:<nik>-<java>") and purl
(pkg:generic/<namespace>/<jdk or nik name>@<version>?package_type=...)
come from the detector. Other vendors are never reported; on the vendor
distributions the apk-installed runtimes under usr/lib/jvm are skipped
because the apk ecosystems cover them. Registered in the JavaArtifact list;
extractor/convert.go derives ecosystem and purl from the new metadata type.

The tests build their runtimes with the module's testfix package; nothing
is checked in.
